Description:

Mailbox sharing over JMAP can now be done the way JMAP Mail Sharing
(draft-ietf-jmap-mail-sharing) says to, with the
urn:ietf:params:jmap:mail:share capability.  It lives with the other
non-standard extensions for now, because the draft hasn't been published yet.

Using that capability, the values in shareWith are MailboxRights objects, the
same shape as myRights, so each right can be granted on its own instead of in
one of the three bundles our own extension offers.

mayRename can be read but not written.  It isn't a right we store anywhere --
it's derived from mayDelete on the mailbox and mayCreateChild on the parent --
so a client may send back the value we gave it, which is what a
read-modify-write of shareWith does, but asking us to change it is forbidden.

The old https://cyrusimap.org/ns/jmap/mail capability for shareWith still
works, and will for a patch version or two.  Each request gets kind of
shareWith it asked for, and the two can't be mixed: mayRead, mayWrite and
mayAdmin are rejected as unknown rights under mail:share, and the MailboxRights
rights are rejected as unknown without it.


